From 4dd7e08aa0fa3f1be141cb4af3abede608835249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaud Pouliquen <arnaud.pouliquen@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 15:20:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: stm32_rproc: Add a fallback method to get the
 boot address

On STM32MP2, the software must provide the ISR vector as the boot address
of the Cortex-M33. The ISR vector table is retrieved by parsing the ELF
file to find the .isr_vectors section.
This method does not work with ELF files that IAR Embedded Workbench
generates because the tool renames the sections.

Add a fallback method that uses the ELF header entry point to find
the boot address.

Change-Id: I7b5ed3368ce6a30929fb9d2a1231311388f5ae28
Signed-off-by: Arnaud Pouliquen <arnaud.pouliquen@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/580513
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Olivier MOYSAN <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/stm32_rproc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_rproc.c b/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_rproc.c
index 0db90005e908..517167645b49 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_rproc.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_rproc.c
@@ -165,7 +165,8 @@ static u64 stm32_rproc_get_vect_table(struct rproc *rproc, const struct firmware
 		return elf_shdr_get_sh_addr(class, shdr);
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	/* The fallback is to get the entry point */
+	return rproc_elf_get_boot_addr(rproc, fw);
 }
 
 static int stm32_rproc_pa_to_da(struct rproc *rproc, phys_addr_t pa, u64 *da)
-- 
2.53.0

